<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Finnic peoples</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Finnic</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Finnic peoples are a group of Uralic-speaking peoples of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eastern-europe">Eastern Europe</a>. Some Finnic and Slavic tribes paid tribute to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar Khaganate</a>, which drew revenue from its dominance over the peoples of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and forest zones.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/finnic-peoples.jpg" alt="Finnic peoples" width="320" height="172" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: GalaxMaps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Finno-Permic_Languages0.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
